# Gate allocator tests by target runtime capabilities, not compile success
id:                     E2183-draft-2301_80739235
trigger_tool:           cmake|ctest|conan-create
phase:                  configure|test|package-validation
error_signature:        "SIGTRAP.*malloc|test_malloc_compliance.*Failed|RLIMIT_AS|malloc.*proxy"
severity:               2
category:               allocator|platform-capability|upstream-tests|runtime
match_keywords:         allocator interposition unsupported, RLIMIT_AS enforcement, malloc proxy SIGTRAP, target CTest capability
root_cause:             Some upstream allocator tests assume glibc allocator interposition or enforceable address-space limits. A non-glibc OHOS runtime can compile these tests but trap during malloc proxy startup or cannot enforce RLIMIT_AS, so compile success is not evidence that the runtime contract exists.
affected_scope:         CMake projects that enable optional allocator proxy tests or memory-limit compliance tests on non-glibc Linux-like targets.
verification_cmd:       Build the normal allocator library, probe the target capability or use a reproducible terminal failure, gate only the unsupported optional tests/components, and run the complete remaining CTest inventory with named exclusions.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           target-runtime-capability-gating
rec_description:        Keep the core allocator and supported tests enabled. Disable the optional malloc proxy component when allocator interposition is unavailable and omit only the address-space compliance test when the target cannot enforce its required limit. Record each excluded test and reason in the target inventory.
rec_command:            "set the CMake component capability in the recipe; guard the exact CTest registration; run the remaining tests"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               cmake-registration-and-toolchain
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      runtime-probe
fallback_description:   When a static capability macro is insufficient, use a bounded target probe for the exact operation and treat probe failure as an explicit unsupported capability, never as a pass.
fallback_command:       "probe allocator interposition or RLIMIT_AS; bind the result to the target test inventory"
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          target-validation
forbid_1_pattern:       "disable.*TBB_TEST|skip.*all.*allocator"
forbid_1_reason:        The core allocator implementation and supported tests remain valid on the target.
forbid_1_consequence:   The package loses meaningful coverage and can hide regressions unrelated to the missing capability.
forbid_2_pattern:       "SIGTRAP.*pass|return.*0.*unsupported"
forbid_2_reason:        A trap or an unexecuted test is not a passing runtime result.
forbid_2_consequence:   CI reports a false target capability claim.
principles:             P007, P015
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
